PROJECT WORKSPACE — Design and complete the iOS frontend for Chats, Files, Tasks, and Notes

We now have the main Project Overview screen with four sections:

* Chats
* Files
* Tasks
* Notes

I want you to take ownership of the iOS UX/UI design for these four sections.

I do NOT have a fixed visual layout for each page. Design them yourself based on the existing BlueMind iOS design language and modern native iOS patterns.

The result should feel like one coherent Project Workspace, not four unrelated screens.

⸻

GLOBAL DESIGN LANGUAGE

Use the BlueMind iOS visual system already established in the app:

* black/dark background
* native iOS spacing and safe areas
* SF Symbols
* native navigation behavior
* subtle Liquid Glass/material where appropriate
* compact floating controls where appropriate
* clean typography
* smooth native transitions
* no Web-looking controls
* no giant cards unless content requires them

Use the existing BlueMind primary color only when an accent is needed:

BLUE_MIND_COLORS.primary

#193B68

Do not introduce random blues.

Keep visual hierarchy simple and premium.

⸻

1. PROJECT CHATS

Design a dedicated Chats page for the current Project.

This page represents conversations belonging specifically to this Project.

I want:

* project-aware header
* list of project conversations
* conversation title
* short preview of latest message
* last updated time/date
* clean empty state
* search when useful
* obvious but compact way to start a new project chat

Tapping a conversation should open that chat.

Starting a new chat from here must create/open a chat associated with the current Project using the existing project/chat capabilities where available.

Do not make it look like an email inbox.

It should feel like BlueMind Chat organized inside a workspace.

Prepare the frontend architecture so project chats can later use Project Files / Notes / Tasks as AI context, but do not invent new backend context behavior if it does not exist yet.

⸻

2. PROJECT FILES

Design a proper Files workspace for the Project.

It should support the existing file functionality available to the Project.

Design for:

* file list/grid as appropriate
* filename
* file type
* size if available
* date
* thumbnails/previews where appropriate
* search
* add/import file
* empty state

Common types should visually make sense:

* PDF
* images
* documents
* text
* other supported files

Tapping a supported file should open a proper preview/viewer.

Do not route the user into an old Web-looking file page if an iOS presentation can be used.

Use the native iOS file picker for adding files where appropriate.

Preserve original file quality.

Do not invent cloud-storage/backend functionality that does not currently exist.

⸻

3. PROJECT TASKS

Build Tasks as a genuinely useful lightweight project task manager.

Design it yourself using native iOS patterns.

At minimum support the existing capabilities for:

* create task
* task title
* completed/not completed
* edit task
* delete task
* task detail if needed

If the current data model already supports them, expose clean controls for:

* due date
* priority
* notes/details

Do NOT add fake backend fields if they are unsupported.

Suggested organization:

To Do

Completed

or another cleaner native solution if you find one.

Completion should have a satisfying subtle native animation.

Do not overbuild this into Jira/Trello.

It should remain fast and simple.

⸻

4. PROJECT NOTES

Build a clean Notes workspace.

It should feel closer to a lightweight native notes app than a form.

Support existing functionality for:

* create note
* title
* body/content
* edit
* delete
* open/read note
* search if appropriate

Notes list should show useful previews rather than giant empty cards.

Editing should be distraction-free with proper keyboard handling and autosave only if the existing architecture safely supports it.

Otherwise use explicit save behavior.

Do not pretend data was saved if the backend request fails.

⸻

5. CONSISTENT PROJECT NAVIGATION

All four pages should clearly remain inside the same Project.

The user should always understand:

I am inside Project X → Chats/Files/Tasks/Notes

Use consistent:

* back behavior
* project title
* navigation
* spacing
* add/create controls
* empty states

Do not create four completely different navigation systems.

⸻

6. GLOBAL BLUE MIND TOASTS

Use the new global iOS toast system for short feedback where available.

Examples:

✓ Task created

✓ Note saved

✓ File added

✓ Chat created

! Upload failed

Do not put giant success boxes inside these pages.

